course: dictionary
lesson: 8378
title: Royal: kings, queens and grand things
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Royal is a describing word, an adjective. Its main meaning is about a king or queen, or their family. «The royal family waved from the palace balcony.» The clues are family and palace, so royal means belonging to a king or queen's family.
explain: Royal can also mean belonging to or working for a king or queen. Many things carry the name Royal, such as the Royal Mail, so you can tell that a word like this is linked to a king or queen, not just to a random thing.
explain: Royal can also mean very grand, fit for a king. «Real lion life is less royal and more teamwork.» The author is saying lion life is less grand than you might expect, because lionesses hunt together and the males guard the land.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. In «a royal welcome», royal means a grand welcome fit for a king. If your meaning makes the sentence sensible, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Royal means about a king or queen, or their family.
fact: Royal can mean belonging to or working for a king or queen.
fact: Royal can mean very grand, fit for a king.
fact: Informally, «a royal» means a member of a royal family, and «the royals» means the royal family.
fact: Useful phrases: royal family, royal palace, a royal welcome, royal blue.
exercise: «Ten royal children jumped merrily along hand in hand.» What does royal tell us about the children? | Pale | *They belong to a king or queen's family | Very quiet | Tall
exercise: What does royal mean in «Real lion life is less royal and more teamwork»? | Hunting at night | *Very grand and fancy, like a king's life | Belonging to a queen | Full of teamwork
exercise: «The Royal Mail delivers letters across the country.» What does Royal tell you about the Royal Mail? | *It is linked to a king or queen | It is a very wet place | It is about giving out light | It is always closed on Sundays
test: «The royal family waved from the balcony.» What does «a royal» mean if someone calls a person «a royal»? | *A member of a royal family | A castle wall | A small dog | A king's crown
test: In «a royal welcome», what does royal mean? | Quiet | Late | Rude | *Very grand, fit for a king
exam: Which meaning fits royal in «the royal family waved from the palace balcony»? | Cold | Wet | *About a king or queen and their family | Very small
